So those were some really great phrases and I think you can play with them a little bit, change some things and then you can use them in your everyday life.

274
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Right.

275
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,280
But why don't we hear them again one more time in context with the dialogue.

276
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,340
Thank God you showed up when you did.

277
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:05,480
He's insane.

278
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,800
Do you think we should call the police?

279
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:09,520
Don't worry about it.

280
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,860
I'll call my friend and have him take care of it.

281
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:14,100
I can't believe he was stalking you all these years.

282
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,400
What a nut job.

283
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:15,840
I know.

284
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:18,360
Well, he said I'm not pregnant.

285
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,200
I'm sorry if I got you all worked up over nothing.

286
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:24,480
I want you to know that I didn't do it on purpose.

287
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:25,340
Don't apologize.

288
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:30,400
From the moment I met you, not a day has gone by when I haven't thought of you.

289
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:34,840
And now that I'm with you again, I'm just scared, Veronica.

290
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:37,000
The closer I get to you, the worse it gets.

291
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:42,100
The thought of not being with you, I mean, I just can't handle it.

292
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,940
We were made for each other, Veronica.

293
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:47,360
You're my everything, my soulmate.

294
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:49,020
What can I do?

295
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,400
Just hold me.

296
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:53,100
I'll always be here for you, no matter what.

297
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:57,460
And together, we can tackle whatever life throws at us.

298
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:59,320
I believe in us, Steven.

299
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:01,720
I'm so happy to hear that.

300
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,500
I know we belong together.

301
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:04,600
I love you so much.

302
00:12:04,670 --> 00:12:05,410
I love you so much.

303
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,240
Okay Erika, so who do you think got shot?

304
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:31,600
I don't know, but I'm starting to think this story is becoming a soap opera.

305
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:37,520
Well, it certainly is and well, what do you guys think happened or who do you think got shot or?

306
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:38,520
Who did the shooting?

307
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,200
Who shot who?

308
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:40,060
Maybe...

309
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:41,520
Was it even a gunshot?

310
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,880
Maybe it was just the car.

311
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:44,800
The tire could have popped.

312
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:45,400
I don't know.

313
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Exactly.

314
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:58,680
So well, come to our website, tell us what you think happens or what you would like to happen because I know many people are expecting a little bit more romance maybe and less drama.

315
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:02,880
But if you have any questions about the language in this lesson, please visit the website at EnglishPod.com.

316
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:03,560
Exactly.

317
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:08,180
Erica and I are always there to answer your questions and well, anything you guys need.

318
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:09,880
Anything?

319
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:10,880
Anything.

320
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:13,880
Well, thanks for listening to this lesson and until next time, goodbye.

